-\subsection{Research question and scope}
+\subsubsection{Continuously varying composition}
+
+A sample whose composition changes continuously contains a range of local spectra. Glycerol solutions provide an example: BFS and linewidth change with concentration \citep{adichtchev2019}. If that relationship is known, the analysis can estimate the concentrations contributing to each measurement. If it is unknown, the analysis must also estimate the relationship between the spectra. This study compares these tasks using simulated data, where the true spectra and contributions are known. Spectral overlap, photon counts and the information supplied to each method can then be varied separately.
+
